  "description": "A parametric WINDOW SEAT on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A NODE OR A SEGMENT. Against a wall segment it takes the wall's direction and the back faces it. This is the plan's box seat under the window — `shoe-rack-with-math` with its top set to Seat is a shoe rack, not this.\n\nTHE LID STYLE DECIDES WHETHER THERE IS A FRONT RAIL. With drawers, the drawers ARE the front, so `_FRONT` drops out — one line, and nothing downstream needs to know.\n\nLID SECTIONS AND DRAWERS ARE THE SAME BROADCAST. `arange(n)` over the length gives every board's near edge, with the reveal taken half from each side so the division always fills the seat exactly whatever the count. A fixed or drawered top is just `n = 1` through the identical expression.\n\nTHE BOLSTERS ARE TUBE ROWS, not prisms — they lie across the depth resting on the cushion at `frameHeight + cushionThk + radius`, so raising the cushion lifts them with it.\n\nEND CHEEKS RUN FROM THE FLOOR, not from the plinth, because in the plan the seat's cheek is the wardrobe's end panel carrying through — a panel that started at the plinth would float.\n\nSTORAGE VOLUME IS REPORTED, NOT DRAWN: the clear box inside the carcass above the base and below the lid. It goes to zero honestly when the frame height is all plinth.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS: 1.524 × 0.610 m, frame top 0.356, seat height 0.458 m (level with a 1'6\" sill), three 0.504 m lid sections, 0.238 m³ of storage, two 0.18 m bolsters.\n\nWHAT THIS CANNOT DO. The lid sections do not open — there is no hinge and no lift angle. Drawer fronts are applied plates with no runners or handles. The cushion is a flat-topped box, not a crowned one.",
